  "behavior": [
    "Forward, reverse and incarnation-keyed TCP collection run as one reserved BPF transaction per candidate. Userspace only enumerates keys.",
    "Expired pending/UDP/SYN/established/closed/reset pairs release their owned return and TCP state. An expired forward cannot delete a foreign return row.",
    "Deleting an obsolete reverse row from the same source epoch preserves the replacement generation TCP key. Old-epoch orphans cannot erase current forward/TCP/return state.",
    "Active TCP metadata missing or bound to a different backend fails closed on request, SYN preflight and reply. It is not reconstructed as legacy; mismatched reset metadata cannot shorten the conservative lifetime.",
    "A v2 scanner visits at most128 keys in each of three maps by default (384 total), saves the next cursor before mutation and defers contended transactions without waiting. It uses a separate program/profile from v1.",
    "Real one-entry map cases recover after pair/orphan collection, including interrupted forward publication and TCP metadata capacity; recovery uses collector transactions, not manual deletion of capacity owners."
  ],
